From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:09:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): session.resume hands the running reply's
 text so far

A viewer that resumed a session mid-reply got the transcript, which does not hold the reply yet, and the frames after the subscription: the reply's start was gone unless the replay ring still held its deltas. The session's event stream now records the running execution's reply text in its current segment under the lock that publishes each frame, and session.resume returns it as inflight_reply {text, sequence}, read under the same lock as last_sequence: the text holds every delta up to sequence and none after, so a viewer shows it and applies only frames after sequence. Absent when no reply text streams.
